entries.officialText:
The unit of intensity of sound is
(A) \text{Wm}^{-2}
(B) \text{Nm}^{-2}
(C) decibel
(D) bel

The area moment of inertia about a diagonal of a square plate of side a is
(A) \frac{a^4}{24}
(B) \frac{a^4}{12}
(C) \frac{a^4}{3}
(D) \frac{a^4}{2}

[Diagram] Range R along the inclined plane (angle of inclination \beta) of a projectile thrown in the vertical plane from the base of the inclined plane with an initial velocity u at an angle \alpha with the horizontal is
(A) \frac{2u^2 \sin(\alpha + \beta) \cos\alpha}{g \cos^2 \beta}
(B) \frac{2u^2 \sin(\alpha - \beta) \cos\alpha}{g \cos^2 \beta}
(C) \frac{u^2 \sin(\alpha - \beta) \cos\alpha}{g \cos\beta}
(D) \frac{u^2 \sin^2(\alpha - \beta) \cos\alpha}{g \cos\beta}

The velocity vs. time graph of a body is a straight line passing through the origin. If the slope of the line is m, the distance travelled by the body in time t from the beginning would be
(A) \frac{t^2}{2m}
(B) \frac{mt^2}{2}
(C) \frac{2mt^2}{3}
(D) mt^2

[Diagram] A ball falling vertically strikes a fixed and frictionless inclined plane, inclined at an angle of 30° to the horizontal, rebounds horizontally as shown. The coefficient of restitution of the ball is
(A) \frac{1}{3}
(B) \frac{1}{4}
(C) \frac{1}{5}
(D) \frac{1}{6}

The elastic constants E (Young's modulus), G (shear modulus) and K (bulk modulus) of a homogeneous and isotropic material are related by
(A) E = \frac{G K}{2K + G}
(B) E = \frac{6G K}{2K + 3G}
(C) E = \frac{9G K}{3K + 2G}
(D) E = \frac{9G K}{3K + G}

A cantilever beam of length L, moment of inertia I, Young's modulus E carries a concentrated load W at the middle of its length. The slope of the cantilever beam at the free end is
(A) \frac{W L^2}{2EI}
(B) \frac{W L^2}{4EI}
(C) \frac{W L^2}{8EI}
(D) \frac{W L^2}{16EI}
